        ":question/id": "a867edc2-7d3a-5fbc-b2ed-43a1f2230791",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-22067",
        ":question/problem": "Let\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhat are the dimensions of $BA?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $BA$ has dimensions $2\\times 2:$\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={BA}_{2\\times 2}\n$$"
      },
