        ":question/id": "cef63f89-6766-5942-a14a-b8ab45d7b4ca",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-320371",
        ":question/problem": "Let\n$E=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$F=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThen, the dimensions of $FE$ are{{field-1}}$\\times $\n{{field-2}}.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We notice that $E$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix and $F$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $F$ and $4$ rows in $E.$ Since the number of columns in $F$ equals the number of rows in $E,$ the matrices $F$ and $E$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $FE$ has dimensions $2\\times 2:$\n\n$$\n{F}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{E}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={FE}_{2\\times 2}\n$$"
      },
