        ":question/id": "9bc6ac30-b2f0-52c3-a082-54b213e2ff6d",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-77476",
        ":question/problem": "Let\n$E=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\sqrt{3} & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhat are the dimensions of $ER?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We notice that $E$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix and $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $E$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $E$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $ER$ has dimensions $3\\times 3:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3}={ER}_{3\\times 3}\n$$"
      }
